@startuml
title squatm3gator API - System Architecture

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam nodesep 35
skinparam ranksep 35
skinparam shadowing false

actor "Web User" as User
actor "Client Application" as Client
actor "Operator" as Operator

rectangle "squatm3gator API Service" {
  component "Web UI Entry\n(index.html @ /)" as WebUI
  component "HTTP API\n(GET /, homoglyph-complete GET,\n400/404/500 plain-text errors)" as API
  component "Session Manager\n(session key = job ID)" as Session
  component "Attack Option Parser\n(Hf, Hc, -add, F, R;\ngodaddy; output)" as Parser
  component "Job Publisher\n(Redis producer)" as Publisher
  component "Background Consumer Thread" as Consumer
  component "squatm3 CLI Wrapper\n(subprocess)" as Squatm3
  component "Reporting Reader\n(session-bound async reporting)" as Reporter
  component "WebSocket / Socket.IO Channel" as Socket
  component "GoDaddy Integration Client\n(optional)" as GoDaddy
  component "Error Handler\n(plain-text messages)" as ErrorHandler
}

package "Redis" as Redis {
  queue "Job Channel" as JobChannel
  queue "Reporting Channel" as ReportChannel
}

cloud "GoDaddy APIs" as GoDaddyAPI

User --> WebUI : GET /
WebUI --> Session : create session
WebUI --> User : rendered index.html
Client --> API : HTTP requests\n(domain, attack codes, flags)
API --> Session : validate session
API --> Parser : parse attack options
Parser --> Publisher : constructed options\n(e.g. -Hf, --add, --output=json)
API --> Publisher : create and publish job\n(job ID = session key)
Publisher --> JobChannel : publish job
JobChannel --> Consumer : job messages
Consumer --> Squatm3 : execute domain generation\nwith constructed CLI options
Squatm3 --> Consumer : domains / progress
Consumer --> ReportChannel : publish worker report
ReportChannel --> Reporter : read report entries
Reporter --> Session : correlate job ID\nwith session key
Reporter --> Socket : emit only matching session
Socket --> Client : async progress / results
Socket --> User : async progress / results

API --> GoDaddy : optional availability check
GoDaddy --> GoDaddyAPI : HTTP\nAuthorization: sso-key <key>:<secret>
GoDaddyAPI --> GoDaddy : availability results
GoDaddy --> API : results

API --> ErrorHandler : HTTP error / query parse failure
ErrorHandler --> Client : plain-text error response

Operator --> Redis : configure Redis URI
Operator --> GoDaddy : configure key, secret,\nbase URL, endpoints

note right of Parser
  Supported attack codes: Hf, Hc, -add, F, R
  Option rule: prefix recognized value with -
  Examples: Hf -> -Hf; -add -> --add
  godaddy == 1 appends GoDaddy option
  output == 1 appends --output=json
end note

note bottom of JobChannel
  Jobs are associated with the requesting session.
  Job ID matches session key (DR-001).
end note

note bottom of ReportChannel
  Worker report format:
  WORKER_ID#JOB_UUID#{MESSAGE/RESULT}
end note

note bottom of API
  GET / returns index.html and creates a session.
  GET homoglyph-complete resource returns
  domains generated by complete homoglyphs attack.
  Query parsing failure returns:
  "Something went wrong while parsing the query string"
end note

@enduml
